    {
     "type": "tip",
     "tag": "Language focus",
     "title": "Crane signals: the verb comes first",
     "steps": [
      [
       "Up",
       "Hoist. Hoist slowly."
      ],
      [
       "Down",
       "Lower. Lower slowly."
      ],
      [
       "Sideways",
       "Slew left. Slew right."
      ],
      [
       "Stop",
       "Stop!"
      ]
     ],
     "paras": [
      "Signals to the crane driver are short orders: the verb first, no <b>you</b>, no <b>please</b>.",
      "Add <b>slowly</b> after the verb when you need it. <b>Slew</b> = the crane turns, so the load goes left or right."
